# Scoring model

Point value is a **rebalanced hybrid** in a single visible config (`scoring-weights.ts`).
All weights live in that config and must be surfaced in the UI breakdown.

Dimensions and intended weight:
- **Rarity / scarcity** — largest (Grade tier + promo/event status)
- **Popularity** — large; franchise-wide, **species-level** (joined by species, not per-tag).
  Source: Species Popularity Table (Notion). Captures e.g. Mewtwo > Arceus.
- **Market price** — SMALL (~15–20%), sanity anchor only. Taiwan resale data is thin/noisy;
  do not let it dominate. Pure-market scoring was deliberately rejected (see ADR 0002).
- **Special-mechanic bonus** — small (Gigantamax/Mega/Z-move/Legendary/Paradox)

Fairness verdict uses tolerance bands (baseline <30% fair / 30–100% richer / >2× unfair),
tunable in config. Never hardcode magic numbers in components — read from config.
Keep the model explainable: a parent/kid should see why a trade is flagged.
